⸻

Objective:

Develop a scheduled refund processing module that triggers paymode-wise and channel bank-wise. It will either invoke a refund API or generate a refund file based on configuration, handle retries, track statuses, and interact with Kafka for status publishing.

⸻

Technical Overview:

1. Module Responsibility
	•	Process refund for one paymode + one channel bank at a time.
	•	Fetch all eligible refund records.
	•	Based on configuration:
	•	Call Refund API via WebClient
	•	OR generate refund CSV file and upload it to SFTP
	•	Track success/failure
	•	Retry up to 3 times if refund fails.
	•	Update statuses and publish results to Kafka.

⸻

Flow Steps:

✅ Scheduler:
	•	Cron job to run at configured intervals.
	•	For each job run:
	•	Accept Paymode & Channel Bank as input.
	•	Trigger refund processing for given paymode + channel bank.

✅ Fetch Refund Records:
	•	From refund_booking table.
	•	Conditions:
	•	refund_status in ("Refund Booked", "Cancellation_Booked")
	•	refund_retry > 0

✅ Refund Processing Logic:
	•	Based on configuration (refund_mode_config table or service):
	•	If API Mode:
	•	Call Refund API via WebClient
	•	Parse response → mark REFUND_PROCESSED on success
	•	If File Mode:
	•	Create Refund CSV
	•	Upload to SFTP
	•	Mark REFUND_PROCESSED on successful upload

✅ Retry Logic:
	•	Maintain refund_retry (int, default 3) in refund_booking.
	•	On failure, decrement refund_retry by 1.
	•	Only fetch and retry records with refund_retry > 0.

✅ Chargeback Scenario:
	•	If chargeback_amount > 0:
	•	Check: refund_amount <= (total_amount - chargeback_amount)
	•	If not, mark as REFUND_FAILED with remark: Exceeds Refundable Limit.

✅ Kafka Integration:
	•	After each refund processing (success or failure):
	•	Publish message to Kafka topic: refund-processing-status
	•	Payload:

{
  "arrn": "ARRN12345",
  "refundStatus": "REFUND_PROCESSED",
  "remark": "Processed via API" // or "Failed due to ...",
  "channelBank": "XYZ",
  "paymode": "UPI"
}



✅ Transaction Service Consumer:
	•	Listens to refund-processing-status topic.
	•	Updates transaction status accordingly.

⸻

Database Changes:

refund_booking Table:

Column Name	Type	Description
refund_retry	INT	Default 3, decremented on each failure
refund_status	TEXT	Tracks processing status
remark	TEXT	Optional remarks for failures/success


